{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And she cast the child</b> — the thirst overpowered him and he could not walk, so his mother laid him under the tree, cast down and abandoned. Or it is like the usage of \"and He cast them to another land\" (Deuteronomy 29:27), \"cast me not away from before You\" (Psalms 51:13) — the meaning being that of sending away. And Rabbi Abraham said, \"and she cast\" — because she took him in her lap when he grew faint from thirst. And our Sages said (Bereshit Rabbah 53:13) that he was ill at the time she sent him away, and she placed the child on her shoulder, and this is the meaning of \"and she cast.\" And all this affair came about for Abraham because he was commanded to do all that Sarah would say, and she commanded to expel him from the household, and by her decree he gave them no silver or gold or servants or camels to carry them."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:32:44.209945018Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}